Malcolm Ryan wrote:
> I've been slowly putting pieces together to create the Alchemist role.
> I've decided on the following:
> 
> Quest artefact: the Philosopher's Stone (can create lots of potions)
> Quest leader: the Comte de Saint Germain
> Quest nemesis: Dr Jekyll / Mr Hyde (a shape-changer)
> 
> The quest levels are going to be sewers with lots of rats, blobs,
> puddings and gelatinous cubes, plus the occasional crocodile. I need
> something special for the "locate" level of the quest. Any
> suggestions?
> 
> Malcolm
> 
Chameleons -- lots of chameleons. Ravens?
Pools of acid -- just like lava only slower. Poisonous fumes boiling off 
the surface. Poison resistance required. Water walking has a 40% chance 
per square of rotting your boots. Completely rotted boots provide no 
acid protection.
Lots of sinks; but no foocubi. Nemesis surrounded by a ring (or two) of 
sinks.
(Rings available only 10% of the sinks.)


